<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- April 11-13.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- April 11-13.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the April 11-13 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Anaconda		   $16,620,887	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. Liar Liar		  $14,486,385	 $120,015,240</p>
<p>3. The Saint		  $10,807,568	 $ 31,401,797</p>
<p>4. Grosse Pointe Blank    $ 6,870,397	 $  ----</p>
<p>5. The Devil's Own	  $ 4,180,149	 $ 35,551,865</p>
<p>6. That Old Feeling	 $ 3,461,835	 $ 10,090,075</p>
<p>7. Jungle 2 Jungle	  $ 2,223,249	 $ 50,986,354</p>
<p>8. Double Team		$ 2,108,589	 $  8,410,614</p>
<p>9. Scream		     $ 2,016,006	 $ 88,826,827</p>
<p>10 Selena		     $ 1,809,611	 $ 30,460,690</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Anaconda,&quot; &quot;The Devil's Own&quot; and &quot;Double Team&quot; are released by Sony Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; and &quot;That Old Feeling&quot; are released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;The Saint&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Grosse Pointe Blank,&quot; &quot;Jungle 2 Jungle&quot; and &quot;The 6th Man&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Scream&quot; is released by Disney's Miramax Films. &quot;Selena&quot; is released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
